# --- Copyrighted game data ---
# Never commit the original N-Gage install image or anything extracted
# straight from it (audio, scripts, textures, the binary itself).
/The-Elder-Scrolls-Travels-Shadowkey_N-Gage_EN-FR-DE-ES-IT_USA-Europe-EnFrDeEsIt-26102004/

# --- Third-party tooling ---
# Not project source; fetched/installed locally, not tracked in git.
/tools/*
!/tools/README.md
!/tools/e32image.py
!/tools/resolve_imports.py
!/tools/fingerprint_compiler.py
!/tools/parse_symbian_lib.py
!/tools/resolve_import_names.py
!/tools/parse_model_resource.py

# --- Ghidra project (regenerable from the .app via tools/e32image.py + analyzeHeadless) ---
# Recursive (**) because pyghidra's open_program(), if nested_project_location
# ever isn't passed as False, silently creates a second, nested, empty project
# tree (shadowkey/ghidra/ShadowkeyProject/ShadowkeyProject.gpr) alongside the
# real top-level one -- happened once already, keep the pattern robust to it.
/shadowkey/ghidra/**/*.gpr
/shadowkey/ghidra/**/*.rep/
/shadowkey/ghidra/**/*.lock*

# --- Extracted/derived binary artifacts (regenerable from the baserom) ---
/shadowkey/extracted/*.bin
/shadowkey/extracted/*.json
/shadowkey/extracted/*.c
# NOTE: shadowkey/import_names.json is NOT under extracted/ and IS tracked
# on purpose -- it's a small, derived (dll!ordinal -> mangled name) table,
# not a copy of the SDK it was cross-referenced against. See
# docs/IMPORT_NAMES.md for provenance and how to regenerate/extend it.
# The SDK itself (third-party, copyrighted install media) is never
# downloaded into this repo -- it lives outside it, path documented in
# that same doc, re-fetch it there if the table ever needs regenerating.

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
